or regressions or failed rubrics, append one root-cause hypothesis under `Failures / Regressions`.\n7. Before exit, append final status (`rubric_pass`, `cap_reached`, or task-specific stop reason) and next hypothesis under `Next Hypotheses`.\n8. When command execution is unavailable, use read/edit/write tools to append directly\nto the required markdown and JSONL files. Preserve all existing content. When command\nexecution is available, prefer the helper for deterministic dual-write:\n- script: detect the active agent config directory first, then use `<that-dir>/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py`\n- command template:\n```bash\nMEMORY_HELPER=\"$(find ./.claude ./.codex ./.cursor ./.opencode ./.gemini ./.pi -path '*/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py' -print -quit 2>/dev/null)\"\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" \\\n  --global-memory-md \"./global_memory/memory.md\" \\\n  --global-memory-jsonl \"./global_memory/memory.jsonl\" \\\n  --event-json '{\"step\":\"evaluate\",\"scope\":\"attempt\",\"summary\":\"...\",\"evidence\":\"...\",\"next_action\":\"...\",\"attempt_id\":\"{{ATTEMPT_ID}}\",\"idea_id\":\"{{IDEA_ID}}\",\"program_id\":\"program_2\",\"metrics\":{\"combined_score\":2.54,\"correct\":true}}'\n```\n9. JSONL event schema (required keys):\n- `timestamp` (auto-filled if omitted)\n- `step` (`idea|edit|evaluate|verify|paper|draft|final|conclusions_skip`)\n- `scope` (`idea|attempt|paper|campaign`)\n- `summary`\n- `evidence`\n- `next_action`\n- optional: `idea_id`, `attempt_id`, `program_id`, `metrics`, `rubrics`, `tags`\n\n10. Update distilled conclusions (`conclusions.md`).\n**Purpose.** `conclusions.md` is a *forward-looking guide* for the next worker (or your future self in a later cycle). Its job is to help readers (a) focus their effort on directions you've found promising, and (b) avoid spending compute on directions you've already shown to be unpromising. Each sentence should either point at a lead worth pursuing or warn against a dead end, framed so a researcher who has not read your `memory.md` can still act on it. Avoid chronology, restate-of-results, and post-mortem narration — those belong in `memory.md`. Conclusions are the synthesis layer that makes other workers' next cycles more efficient.\n\n**When.** After every memory-append in the cycle (idea / edit / evaluate / verify / paper / final), evaluate whether `conclusions.md` should be updated.\n\n**Update gate (the only valid triggers).**\n- (a) cycle **contradicts** an existing sentence → rewrite that sentence.\n- (b) cycle opens a **new category** not yet covered → add a sentence.\n- (c) cycle **flips a Do/Don't** recommendation → flip it.\n- (d) cycle **meaningfully refines** an existing sentence — narrows the conditions under which a rule holds, broadens its applicability to a config it wasn't known to apply to, sharpens a tentative claim into a confident one, or adds a qualifier the prior phrasing didn't cover → edit the sentence to incorporate the refinement. Simple re-confirmation in the same regime is **not** sufficient; you must identify the refinement dimension (narrow / broaden / sharpen / qualify) in `--gate-reason`.\n- otherwise → **keep**, do not invoke the helper.\n\n**Format constraints.** Single paragraph. ≤300 words. No blank lines (`\\n\\n`). Avoid detailed numerical figures — use qualitative thresholds (e.g. \"low LR\", \"small batch\") instead of precise floats like `LR=0.205`.\n\n**Update mechanism.** When execution is unavailable, apply the same validation rules\nand update the conclusions files directly with read/edit/write tools. When execution\nis available, use this helper invocation:\n```bash\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" --write-conclusions \\\n  --conclusions-md \"{{CONCLUSIONS_MD_FILE}}\" \\\n  --conclusions-history-jsonl \"{{CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_FILE}}\" \\\n  --cycle-index {{CYCLE_INDEX}} \\\n  --worker-index {{WORKER_INDEX}} \\\n  --gate-trigger <a|b|c|d> \\\n  --gate-reason \"<one sentence; for (d) name the dimension>\" \\\n  --conclusions-text \"<the full new paragraph>\"\n```\n\n**Pre-flight self-check.** Before invoking the helper, count words (`len(paragraph.split())`) and confirm ≤300, and that the paragraph contains no blank line. Most validation rejections can be avoided here.\n\n**Retry budget — exactly 3 attempts per cycle.** On non-zero exit, read the stderr error, shorten the paragraph (drop the least-decisive sentence, merge two related sentences, or remove qualifiers), and retry. After **3 total attempts** with no success, the update is **discarded** for this cycle: do not retry further, do not write the rejected text anywhere, and append a single memory event with `step=\"conclusions_skip\"` whose `summary` names the last validation error. Underlying findings are not lost — they are already durable in `memory.md`.\n\n**Always log the gate decision.** Inside the regular memory append for the cycle, include `gate=<updated|kept|skipped>; trigger=<a|b|c|d|none>; reason=<one sentence>` in the entry's `summary` or `tags`. Use `skipped` only after the 3-attempt budget is exhausted.\n\n# Example evaluation entry\n```markdown\n### 2026-02-13T16:58:00Z | step=evaluate\n- program: program_3\n- combined_score: 2.54\n- correct: true\n- rubrics: uses_restarts=pass, constraint_optimization=pass, score_threshold=fail\n- evidence: late-stage overlap still visible in stdout trace\n- next_recommendation: raise late-stage overlap penalty and diversify restart seeds\n```\n\n--- FILES ---\n.\n..\n.agentic_paper_workspace.json\n.codex\n.paper_figure_quality_repair_stream_20261107_044409.fifo\n.paper_two_stage_enabled\n.postdraft_reference_enrichment_complete\nREPRODUCIBILITY.md\nVENUE.md\nanalysis_results.json\nanalysis_results.json.prov.json\nbibtex.log\nclaims_grounding.json\ncompilation.log\nconcept_figure_run.log\ndraft_reference_gaps.json\ndraft_reference_gaps.md\ndraft_reference_gaps_agent_codex_20261107_044409.log\ndraft_reference_gaps_prompt.md\ndraft_reference_gaps_validation_feedback.json\ndraft_reference_gaps_validation_feedback.md\nfigure_manifest.json\nfigures\nglobal_memory\nglobal_memory_recent.json\nglobal_memory_summary.md\niclr2026_conference.bst\niclr2026_conference.sty\nliterature\nlocal_validation_report.json\nmemory.md\npaper.aux\npaper.bbl\npaper.blg\npaper.bst\npaper.fls\npaper.log\npaper.out\npaper.pdf\npaper.sty\npaper.tex\npaper_agent_codex_20261107_044409.log\npaper_data.json\npaper_diagnostics\npaper_diagnostics_20261107_044409_197126.log\npaper_events_20261107_044409.jsonl\npaper_evidence_audit.json\npaper_evidence_audit.md\npaper_evidence_audit_agent_codex_20261107_044409.log\npaper_evidence_audit_agent_codex_20261107_044409_round_2.log\npaper_evidence_audit_feedback.json\npaper_evidence_audit_feedback.md\npaper_evidence_audit_input_sha256.json\npaper_evidence_audit_packet.md\npaper_evidence_audit_prompt.md\npaper_evidence_audit_prompt_round_2.md\npaper_evidence_audit_raw.txt\npaper_figure_quality_repair_agent_codex_20261107_044409.log\npaper_figure_quality_repair_prompt.md\npaper_prep_20261107_044409.json\npaper_prompt.md\npaper_repair_agent_codex_20261107_044409_round_1.log\npaper_repair_prompt_round_1.md\npaper_strategy.json\npaper_strategy.md\npaper_strategy_agent_codex_20261107_044409.log\npaper_strategy_prompt.md\npaper_strategy_resolution.json\nreference_query_plan.json\nreference_query_plan.md\nreference_query_plan_agent_codex_20261107_044409.log\nreference_query_plan_prompt.md\nreference_query_plan_validation_feedback.json\nreference_query_plan_validation_feedback.md\nreference_retrieval.log\nreferences.bib\nreferences_provenance.json\nrepair_validation_report.json\nreproduction_environment.json\nreproduction_environment.json.prov.json\nresults\nscientific-evidence\nscripts\nsource_evidence\nstrategy_validation_feedback.json\nstrategy_validation_feedback.md\ntables\ntask\nvalidation_feedback.json\nvalidation_feedback.md\nvalidation_report.json\n\n--- MANIFEST ---\n{\n  \"figures\": [\n    {\n      \"attempted_generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\",\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        4\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5,\n      \"fallback_reason\": \"generate-concept-figure exited non-zero (rc=1)\",\n      \"figure_id\": \"frozen_score_overview\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"diagram\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 9,\n        \"legend\": 8.5,\n        \"ticks\": 8.5,\n        \"title\": 9\n      },\n      \"generator\": null,\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 30,\n      \"n_panels\": 1,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 1,\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/frozen_score_overview.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"prompt_log_path\": \"figures/frozen_score_overview.prompts.json\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        2\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        4,\n        4,\n        4,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5,\n      \"figure_id\": \"coverage_width_comparison\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"composite\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 9,\n        \"legend\": 8.5,\n        \"ticks\": 8.5,\n        \"title\": 9\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 30,\n      \"n_panels\": 4,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/coverage_width_comparison.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/coverage_width_comparison.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        4,\n        4,\n        4,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"categories_per_panel\": [\n        4,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5,\n      \"figure_id\": \"rare_outcome_diagnostic\",\n      \"figure_type\": \"composite\",\n      \"font_sizes\": {\n        \"axis\": 9,\n        \"legend\": 8.5,\n        \"ticks\": 8.5,\n        \"title\": 9\n      },\n      \"generator\": \"matplotlib\",\n      \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n      \"max_label_chars\": 30,\n      \"n_panels\": 2,\n      \"panels_per_row\": 2,\n      \"path_pdf\": \"figures/rare_outcome_diagnostic.pdf\",\n      \"path_png\": \"figures/rare_outcome_diagnostic.png\",\n      \"placement\": \"full_width\",\n      \"series_per_panel\": [\n        4,\n        4\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"final.evidence.episodes\"\n      ],\n      \"uses_abbrev_labels\": true,\n      \"uses_progression\": false\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n--- FIGURE CODE ---\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.stats import binomtest, t\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nDATA = ROOT / \"paper_data.json\"\nMETHODS = [\"candidate\", \"ppi_plus_plus_mean\", \"prediction_powered_mean\",\n           \"labeled_only_asymptotic_mean\", \"labeled_only_exact_binomial\"]\nLABELS = [\"Score control\", \"PPI++\", \"PPI\", \"Label normal\", \"Exact binomial\"]\nCOLORS = [\"#007C83\", \"#CB6438\", \"#8E689D\", \"#758195\", \"#31548B\"]\n\n\ndef provenance(path, inputs=None):\n    payload = {\n        \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n        \"artifact\": {\"path\": str(path.relative_to(ROOT)), \"kind\": \"derived\",\n                     \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()},\n        \"derived_from\": inputs or [\"@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\"],\n        \"generated_by\": {\"script_path\": \"scripts/build_artifacts.py\",\n                         \"command\": [\"python\", \"scripts/build_artifacts.py\"]},\n    }\n    Path(str(path) + \".prov.json\").write_text(json.dumps(payload, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef save_panel(figure, name):\n    for extension in [\"pdf\", \"png\"]:\n        path = ROOT / \"figures\" / f\"{name}.{extension}\"\n        figure.savefig(path, dpi=300, facecolor=\"white\")\n        provenance(path)\n    plt.close(figure)\n\n\ndef mean_interval(values):\n    values = np.asarray(values)\n    center = float(values.mean())\n    margin = float(t.ppf(.975, len(values) - 1) * values.std(ddof=1) / np.sqrt(len(values)))\n    return {\"mean\": center, \"lower95\": center - margin, \"upper95\": center + margin}\n\n\ndef main():\n    # @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n    data = json.loads(DATA.read_text())\n    episodes = data[\"final_evaluation\"][\"evaluation_evidence\"][\"episodes\"]\n    summaries = episodes[0][\"solution\"][\"case_summaries\"]\n    results = []\n    for position, reference in enumerate(summaries):\n        records = [episode[\"solution\"][\"cases\"][position] for episode in episodes]\n        assert all(record[\"case\"] == reference[\"case\"] for record in records)\n        truth_values = sorted(set(record[\"truth\"] for record in records))\n        row = {\"case\": reference[\"case\"], \"truths\": truth_values, \"methods\": {}, \"differences\": {}}\n        for method in METHODS:\n            intervals = [record[\"response\"] if method == \"candidate\" else record[\"baselines\"][method] for record in records]\n            widths = np.array([item[\"upper\"] - item[\"lower\"] for item in intervals])\n            covered = np.array([item[\"lower\"] <= record[\"truth\"] <= item[\"upper\"] for item, record in zip(intervals, records)])\n            bounds = binomtest(int(covered.sum()), len(covered)).proportion_ci(method=\"exact\")\n            row[\"methods\"][method] = {\"coverage\": float(covered.mean()), \"covered\": int(covered.sum()),\n                \"coverage_lower95\": float(bounds.low), \"coverage_upper95\": float(bounds.high),\n                \"width\": mean_interval(widths), \"zero_width_count\": int(np.count_nonzero(widths == 0)),\n                \"widths\": widths.tolist()}\n        candidate_widths = np.array(row[\"methods\"][\"candidate\"][\"widths\"])\n        for method in METHODS[1:]:\n            row[\"differences\"][method] = mean_interval(candidate_widths - row[\"methods\"][method][\"widths\"])\n            recorded = reference[\"comparisons\"][method][\"difference\"]\n            assert np.isclose(row[\"differences\"][method][\"mean\"], recorded[\"mean_difference\"], atol=1e-12)\n            assert np.isclose(row[\"differences\"][method][\"lower95\"], recorded[\"lower95\"], atol=1e-10)\n        results.append(row)\n    out = {\"repetitions\": len(episodes), \"seeds\": [episode[\"seed\"] for episode in episodes],\n           \"case_count\": len(results), \"cases\": results,\n           \"interpretation\": \"Pointwise exact binomial coverage intervals; paired t width-difference intervals. No multiplicity correction or new evaluation.\"}\n    path = ROOT / \"analysis_results.json\"\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    provenance(path)\n    headers = \"Condition & Score control & PPI++ & PPI & Label normal & Exact binomial\"\n    coverage_rows = [headers + r\" \\\\\", r\"\\midrule\"]\n    width_rows = [headers + r\" \\\\\", r\"\\midrule\"]\n    for row in results:\n        coverage_rows.append(\"C%d & \" % row[\"case\"] + \" & \".join(f'{row[\"methods\"][method][\"coverage\"]:.3f}' for method in METHODS) + r\" \\\\\")\n        width_rows.append(\"C%d & \" % row[\"case\"] + \" & \".join(f'{row[\"methods\"][method][\"width\"][\"mean\"]:.5f}' for method in METHODS) + r\" \\\\\")\n    for name, rows in [(\"coverage\", coverage_rows), (\"width\", width_rows)]:\n        path = ROOT / \"tables\" / f\"{name}.tex\"\n        path.write_text(\"% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(rows) + \"\\n\\\\bottomrule\\n\")\n        provenance(path)\n    extended = []\n    for row in results:\n        for method, label in zip(METHODS, LABELS):\n            value = row[\"methods\"][method]\n            extended.append(f'C{row[\"case\"]} & {label} & {value[\"coverage\"]:.3f} [{value[\"coverage_lower95\"]:.3f}, {value[\"coverage_upper95\"]:.3f}] & {value[\"width\"][\"mean\"]:.5f} & {value[\"zero_width_count\"]}' + r\" \\\\\")\n        extended.append(r\"\\midrule\")\n    path = ROOT / \"tables\" / \"complete.tex\"\n    path.write_text(\"% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(extended) + \"\\n\\\\bottomrule\\n\")\n    provenance(path)\n    differences = []\n    for row in results:\n        for method, label in zip(METHODS[1:], LABELS[1:]):\n            value = row[\"differences\"][method]\n            differences.append(f'C{row[\"case\"]} & {label} & {value[\"mean\"]:+.6f} & [{value[\"lower95\"]:+.6f}, {value[\"upper95\"]:+.6f}]' + r\" \\\\\")\n        differences.append(r\"\\midrule\")\n    path = ROOT / \"tables\" / \"differences.tex\"\n    path.write_text(\"% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(differences) + \"\\n\\\\bottomrule\\n\")\n    provenance(path)\n    plt.rcParams.update({\"font.size\": 9, \"axes.titlesize\": 9, \"axes.labelsize\": 9,\n                         \"xtick.labelsize\": 8.5, \"ytick.labelsize\": 9,\n                         \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n                         \"pdf.fonttype\": 42, \"ps.fonttype\": 42})\n    plotted = [0, 1, 3, 4]\n    figure, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(5.5, 4.3), gridspec_kw={\"width_ratios\": [1, 1.1]})\n    for group_index, indices in enumerate([range(4), range(4, 7)]):\n        coverage_axis, width_axis = axes[group_index]\n        offsets = np.linspace(-.23, .23, len(plotted))\n        for method_index, offset in zip(plotted, offsets):\n            for local_index, case_index in enumerate(indices):\n                value = results[case_index][\"methods\"][METHODS[method_index]]\n                coverage_axis.errorbar(value[\"coverage\"], local_index + offset,\n                    xerr=[[value[\"coverage\"] - value[\"coverage_lower95\"]], [value[\"coverage_upper95\"] - value[\"coverage\"]]],\n                    fmt=\"o\", ms=3.4, lw=.8, color=COLORS[method_index], capsize=1.5)\n        for method_index, offset in zip([1, 3, 4], [-.18, 0, .18]):\n            for local_index, case_index in enumerate(indices):\n                value = results[case_index][\"differences\"][METHODS[method_index]]\n                width_axis.errorbar(1000 * value[\"mean\"], local_index + offset,\n                    xerr=[[1000 * (value[\"mean\"] - value[\"lower95\"])], [1000 * (value[\"upper95\"] - value[\"mean\"])]],\n                    fmt=\"o\", ms=3.4, lw=.8, color=COLORS[method_index], capsize=1.5)\n        for axis in [coverage_axis, width_axis]:\n            axis.set_yticks(range(len(indices)), [f\"C{position + 1}\" for position in indices])\n            axis.set_ylim(len(indices)-.5, -.5)\n            axis.grid(axis=\"x\", alpha=.13)\n        coverage_axis.axvline(.95, ls=\"--\", lw=.8, color=\"#444444\")\n        coverage_axis.set_xlim((.84, 1.005) if group_index == 0 else (.48, 1.015))\n        width_axis.axvline(0, ls=\"--\", lw=.8, color=\"#444444\")\n    axes[0, 0].set_title(\"(a) Coverage: C1–C4\", loc=\"left\")\n    axes[0, 1].set_title(\"(b) Width differences: C1–C4\", loc=\"left\")\n    axes[1, 0].set_title(\"(c) Coverage: C5–C7\", loc=\"left\")\n    axes[1, 1].set_title(\"(d) Width differences: C5–C7\", loc=\"left\")\n    axes[1, 0].set_xlabel(\"Empirical coverage\")\n    axes[1, 1].set_xlabel(\"Width difference (×10⁻³)\")\n    handles = [plt.Line2D([], [], color=COLORS[index], marker=\"o\", ms=4, lw=1, label=LABELS[index]) for index in plotted]\n    figure.legend(handles=handles, loc=\"upper center\", ncol=2, frameon=False, fontsize=9, bbox_to_anchor=(.51, 1.005))\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.09, right=.98, bottom=.13, top=.79, wspace=.46, hspace=.62)\n    save_panel(figure, \"coverage_width_comparison\")\n    figure, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(5.5, 2.3), gridspec_kw={\"width_ratios\": [1.25, 1]})\n    rare = results[4]\n    for method_index in [0, 1, 2, 4]:\n        values = np.sort(rare[\"methods\"][METHODS[method_index]][\"widths\"])\n        axes[0].step(np.r_[0, values], np.r_[0, np.arange(1, len(values)+1)/len(values)], where=\"post\", color=COLORS[method_index], lw=1.25, label=LABELS[method_index])\n    axes[0].set(xlabel=\"Interval width\", ylabel=\"Empirical CDF\", ylim=(0, 1.03), xlim=(0, None))\n    axes[0].set_title(\"(a) C5 width distribution\", loc=\"left\")\n    selected = [0, 1, 2, 4]\n    counts = [rare[\"methods\"][METHODS[index]][\"zero_width_count\"] for index in selected]\n    axes[1].barh(range(4), counts, color=[COLORS[index] for index in selected], height=.6)\n    axes[1].set_yticks(range(4), [LABELS[index] for index in selected], fontsize=8.5)\n    axes[1].invert_yaxis()\n    axes[1].set_xlim(0, max(counts)*1.25)\n    axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Zero-width intervals\")\n    for position, count in enumerate(counts):\n        axes[1].text(count + 2, position, str(count), va=\"center\", fontsize=9)\n    axes[1].set_title(\"(b) Collapse counts\", loc=\"left\")\n    handles, labels = axes[0].get_legend_handles_labels()\n    figure.legend(handles, labels, loc=\"upper center\", ncol=4, frameon=False, fontsize=8.5, bbox_to_anchor=(.5, 1.015), handlelength=1.2, columnspacing=.9)\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.1, right=.99, bottom=.24, top=.73, wspace=.67)\n    save_panel(figure, \"rare_outcome_diagnostic\")\n    concept = ROOT / \"figures\" / \"frozen_score_overview.png\"\n    prompt_log = concept.with_suffix(\".prompts.json\")\n    if not (ROOT / \".concept_figure_complete\").exists() and not concept.exists():\n        from PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n        image = Image.new(\"RGB\", (2400, 630), \"white\")\n        draw = ImageDraw.Draw(image)\n        draw.text((50, 280), \"Concept figure reserved for synchronous rendering\", fill=\"#666666\")\n        image.save(concept)\n    if not prompt_log.exists():\n        prompt_log.write_text(\"{}\\n\")\n    figures = []\n    specifications = {item[\"figure_id\"]: item for item in\n                      json.loads((ROOT / \"paper_strategy.json\").read_text())[\"figure_specs\"]}\n    for name, panels, categories, series, height in [\n        (\"frozen_score_overview\", 1, 4, 2, 1.8),\n        (\"coverage_width_comparison\", 4, 4, 4, 4.3),\n        (\"rare_outcome_diagnostic\", 2, 4, 4, 2.3)]:\n        entry = {\"figure_id\": name, \"path_png\": f\"figures/{name}.png\",\n                 \"figure_type\": specifications[name][\"figure_type\"],\n                 \"n_panels\": panels, \"panels_per_row\": 1 if panels == 1 else 2,\n                 \"categories_per_panel\": [categories] * panels, \"series_per_panel\": [series] * panels,\n                 \"max_label_chars\": 30, \"font_sizes\": {\"title\": 9, \"axis\": 9, \"legend\": 8.5, \"ticks\": 8.5},\n                 \"uses_abbrev_labels\": True, \"uses_progression\": False,\n                 \"source_ids\": [] if panels == 1 else [\"final.evidence.episodes\"],\n                 \"generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\" if panels == 1 else \"matplotlib\",\n                 \"placement\": \"full_width\", \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n                 \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5}\n        if panels == 1:\n            entry[\"prompt_log_path\"] = f\"figures/{name}.prompts.json\"\n        else:\n            entry[\"path_pdf\"] = f\"figures/{name}.pdf\"\n        figures.append(entry)\n    (ROOT / \"figure_manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"figures\": figures}, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    for row in results:\n        print(\"C\", row[\"case\"], \"truth\", row[\"truths\"], \"coverage\", row[\"methods\"][\"candidate\"][\"coverage\"], \"width\", row[\"methods\"][\"candidate\"][\"width\"][\"mean\"], \"PPI++ difference\", row[\"differences\"][METHODS[1]])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n--- CHECKER ---\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport jsonschema\nimport pymupdf\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\n\ndef main():\n    data = json.loads((ROOT / \"paper_data.json\").read_text())\n    strategy = json.loads((ROOT / \"paper_strategy.json\").read_text())\n    manifest = json.loads((ROOT / \"figure_manifest.json\").read_text())\n    schema = json.loads((ROOT / \".codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\").read_text())\n    jsonschema.validate(manifest, schema)\n    specifications = {item[\"figure_id\"]: item for item in strategy[\"figure_specs\"]}\n    manuscript = (ROOT / \"paper.tex\").read_text()\n    declared_paths = set()\n    for figure in manifest[\"figures\"]:\n        spec = specifications[figure[\"figure_id\"]]\n        assert figure[\"figure_type\"] == spec[\"figure_type\"], figure[\"figure_id\"]\n        assert figure[\"n_panels\"] <= spec[\"max_panels\"]\n        assert max(figure[\"categories_per_panel\"]) <= spec[\"max_categories_per_panel\"]\n        assert max(figure[\"series_per_panel\"]) <= spec[\"max_series_per_panel\"]\n        assert figure[\"panels_per_row\"] <= spec[\"max_panels_per_row\"]\n        assert figure[\"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\"] >= 8\n        assert set(figure[\"source_ids\"]) <= set(data[\"grounding_sources\"])\n        for field in [\"path_png\", \"path_pdf\", \"prompt_log_path\"]:\n            if field in figure:\n                assert (ROOT / figure[field]).is_file()\n                declared_paths.add(figure[field])\n    for included in re.findall(r\"\\\\includegraphics(?:\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\{([^}]+)\\}\", manuscript):\n        assert included in declared_paths, included\n    assert set(specifications) == {item[\"figure_id\"] for item in manifest[\"figures\"]}\n    resolved_json = 0\n    resolved_lines = 0\n    for token in re.findall(r\"@evidence\\[\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\]\", manuscript):\n        target, separator, locator = token.partition(\"#\")\n        path = ROOT / target\n        assert path.is_file(), token\n        if path.suffix == \".json\" and locator.startswith(\"/\"):\n            value = json.loads(path.read_text())\n            for part in locator[1:].split(\"/\"):\n                part = part.replace(\"~1\", \"/\").replace(\"~0\", \"~\")\n                value = value[int(part)] if isinstance(value, list) else value[part]\n            resolved_json += 1\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"L\\d+(?:-L?\\d+)?\", locator):\n            numbers = [int(value) for value in re.findall(r\"\\d+\", locator)]\n            assert max(numbers) <= len(path.read_text().splitlines()), token\n            resolved_lines += 1\n    pdf = pymupdf.open(ROOT / \"paper.pdf\")\n    texts = [page.get_text() for page in pdf]\n    reference_index = next(index for index, text in enumerate(texts) if re.search(r\"\\bREFERENCES\\b\", text))\n    supplement_index = next(index for index, text in enumerate(texts) if \"SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION\" in text)\n    assert reference_index in [8, 9], reference_index\n    assert supplement_index > reference_index\n    assert \"LLM USAGE\" in \"\\n\".join(texts)\n    forbidden = r\"\\b(?:ideas?|programs?|attempts?|eligible|worker_01|worker_02|combined_score|rubric)\\b\"\n    for page_text in texts:\n        scrubbed = re.sub(r\"program\\.py\", \"source-file\", page_text)\n        assert not re.search(forbidden, scrubbed, re.I), re.search(forbidden, scrubbed, re.I)\n    body_last = pdf[reference_index - 1]\n    rectangles = []\n    for block in body_last.get_text(\"dict\")[\"blocks\"]:\n        for line in block.get(\"lines\", []):\n            spans = [span for span in line[\"spans\"] if span[\"bbox\"][0] >= 106 and span[\"bbox\"][2] <= 506\n                     and 70 <= span[\"bbox\"][1] < 730 and not span[\"text\"].isdigit()]\n            rectangles.extend(span[\"bbox\"] for span in spans)\n    extent = max(rectangle[3] for rectangle in rectangles) - min(rectangle[1] for rectangle in rectangles)\n    fill = extent / 648\n    assert fill >= .75 if reference_index == 8 else True\n    specification = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"rendered_si\", ROOT / \".codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\")\n    validator = importlib.util.module_from_spec(specification)\n    specification.loader.exec_module(validator)\n    body_texts = [page.get_text(clip=pymupdf.Rect(105, 65, 507, 750), sort=True) for page in pdf]\n    errors = validator.validate_rendered_supplementary_information(body_texts)\n    assert not errors, errors\n    summary = json.loads((ROOT / \"scientific-evidence/verification-report.json\").read_text())[\"summary\"]\n    assert summary[\"dangling_references\"] == 0\n    report = {\"status\": \"local_checks_passed\", \"body_pages\": reference_index, \"total_pages\": len(pdf),\n              \"last_body_page_vertical_extent_fraction\": fill,\n              \"geometry_note\": \"Local text-span extent, excluding margin counters; not the parent orchestrator's authoritative occupancy metric.\",\n              \"figure_schema\": \"passed\", \"strategy_figure_budgets\": \"passed\", \"figures\": len(manifest[\"figures\"]),\n              \"resolved_manuscript_json_pointers\": resolved_json, \"resolved_source_line_locators\": resolved_lines,\n              \"rendered_supplement\": \"passed canonical heading/content function on PyMuPDF text within the official text frame\",\n              \"dangling_evidence_references\": 0,\n              \"canonical_tooling_limits\": [\n                  \"Standalone figure-validator entrypoint cannot import the absent parent src.orchestrator module; canonical JSON schema and strategy budgets checked locally.\",\n                  \"compile_latex.sh recorder checker rejects a system texmf.cnf symlink crossing two approved TeX roots. Sanitized pdflatex/BibTeX commands compile successfully; parent revalidation remains authoritative.\",\n                  \"System pdftotext is unavailable. Rendered SI checked from independent PyMuPDF extraction within the official text frame, excluding margin counters.\",\n                  \"Concept image is an orchestrator-owned placeholder until synchronous post-draft rendering.\"\n              ]}\n    (ROOT / \"local_validation_report.json\").write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n--- LATEX FIGURES ---\n19:\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,booktabs,graphicx,subcaption,longtable}\n49:\\begin{figure}[t]\n53:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth,height=1.8in,keepaspectratio]{figures/frozen_score_overview.png}\n55:\\caption{Inference with unchanged observations and a frozen predictor. Complementary labeled folds fit score-only controls; held-out residual correction targets the population mean. The evaluated stabilized asymptotic interval and the separate, unmeasured bounded safety construction must not be conflated. No new labels or predictor training are part of this comparison.}\n58:\\end{figure}\n174:\\caption{Empirical coverage. Every condition has 256 repetitions and nominal coverage 0.95. Pointwise uncertainty is plotted in Figure~\\ref{fig:comparison} and fully tabulated in Supplementary Information. The low coverage of evaluated PPI++ and labeled normal inference in C5 remains visible.}\n186:\\caption{Mean interval width on the population-mean scale. Smaller values are not automatically preferable when coverage differs. PPI++ is slightly wider than score control only in C2; the exact-binomial comparison in C5 is unresolved by paired uncertainty.}\n202:\\begin{figure}[t]\n204:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/coverage_width_comparison.pdf}\n205:\\caption{Coverage and paired width differences across all conditions. (a,c) Empirical coverage with pointwise 95\\% exact-binomial limits; dashed lines indicate nominal coverage. (b,d) Score-control minus comparator mean widths with paired-$t$ limits; negative values mean narrower. Colors identify the comparator in width panels and the interval method in coverage panels. Coverage and width scales differ between rows. PPI is retained in the tables and Figure~\\ref{fig:rare}. No interval here is multiplicity-adjusted.}\n208:\\end{figure}\n211:Score-control coverage ranges from $0.929688$ in C5 to $0.957031$ in C3. The pooled recorded coverage is $0.942522$, and the pooled mean width is $0.129888$. These aggregates describe the evaluated mix of conditions, not a population of application domains. They cannot replace the condition-specific comparisons, and we do not attach an independence-based binomial interval to the pooled figure.\n228:\\begin{figure}[t]\n230:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth]{figures/rare_outcome_diagnostic.pdf}\n231:\\caption{C5 rare-outcome diagnostic, using all 256 endpoint records. (a) Empirical CDFs retain the mass at zero on a linear width axis. (b) Collapsed-interval counts. Labeled normal inference, omitted from this four-method display, also has 115 zero-width intervals. The associated coverage values appear in Table~\\ref{tab:coverage}. Avoiding collapse does not establish nominal coverage or superiority to exact-binomial inference.}\n234:\\end{figure}\n271:\\caption{Complete marginal interval summaries. Limits in brackets are pointwise 95\\% coverage intervals; $Z$ is the count of zero-width intervals.}\\label{tab:complete}\\\\\n327:\\caption{Paired score-control minus comparator width differences. Negative values indicate narrower recorded intervals, not a coverage-adjusted advantage.}\\label{tab:paired}\\\\\n442:The read-only \\path{paper_data.json} is the primary numerical input. The script \\path{scripts/build_artifacts.py} reads the final endpoint records, checks paired differences against the supplied summaries, and writes \\path{analysis_results.json}, the tables under \\path{tables/}, and both quantitative figure groups under \\path{figures/}. Each quantitative figure is exported as vector PDF and 300-DPI PNG, with an adjacent provenance sidecar recording its inputs. The overview figure is separately prepared from the method description and is not a quantitative result plot.\n\n--- VALIDATOR FILES ---\n.codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\n.codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/SKILL.md\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_compile_inputs.py\n.codex/skills/retrieve-references/templates/provenance.schema.json\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\n.codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/templates/claims_grounding.schema.json\n.codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/__pycache__/validate_rendered_si.cpython-312.pyc\n\n--- GIT ---\nfatal: not a git repository (or any parent up to mount point /)\nStopping at filesystem boundary (GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM not set).\n","exit_code":128,"status":"failed"}}
