{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"sed -n '1,230p' scripts/build_artifacts.py; printf '\\\\n--- LOCAL VALIDATION ---\\\\n'; cat scripts/check_paper.py; printf '\\\\n--- CONCEPT SOURCE CANDIDATES ---\\\\n'; rg -n --hidden 'frozen_score_overview|ImageDraw|draw\\\\.rectangle|drawio|PIL' --glob '\"'!paper_data.json'\"' --glob '\"'!memory.md'\"' --glob '\"'!*.jsonl'\"' --glob '\"'!*.log'\"' --glob '\"'!*.aux'\"' --glob '\"'!*.fdb_latexmk'\"' . | head -100; printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY / CONCLUSIONS ---\\\\n'; tail -35 memory.md; ls global_memory; cat conclusions.md; printf '\\\\n--- PARENT / MODULES ---\\\\n'; ls /workspace; printf '\\\\n--- COMPILE ---\\\\n'; sed -n '1,160p' .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh\"","aggregated_output":"import hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.stats import binomtest, t\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nDATA = ROOT / \"paper_data.json\"\nMETHODS = [\"candidate\", \"ppi_plus_plus_mean\", \"prediction_powered_mean\",\n           \"labeled_only_asymptotic_mean\", \"labeled_only_exact_binomial\"]\nLABELS = [\"Score control\", \"PPI++\", \"PPI\", \"Label normal\", \"Exact binomial\"]\nCOLORS = [\"#007C83\", \"#CB6438\", \"#8E689D\", \"#758195\", \"#31548B\"]\n\n\ndef provenance(path, inputs=None):\n    payload = {\n        \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n        \"artifact\": {\"path\": str(path.relative_to(ROOT)), \"kind\": \"derived\",\n                     \"sha256\": hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()},\n        \"derived_from\": inputs or [\"@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\"],\n        \"generated_by\": {\"script_path\": \"scripts/build_artifacts.py\",\n                         \"command\": [\"python\", \"scripts/build_artifacts.py\"]},\n    }\n    Path(str(path) + \".prov.json\").write_text(json.dumps(payload, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n\n\ndef save_panel(figure, name):\n    for extension in [\"pdf\", \"png\"]:\n        path = ROOT / \"figures\" / f\"{name}.{extension}\"\n        figure.savefig(path, dpi=300, facecolor=\"white\")\n        provenance(path)\n    plt.close(figure)\n\n\ndef mean_interval(values):\n    values = np.asarray(values)\n    center = float(values.mean())\n    margin = float(t.ppf(.975, len(values) - 1) * values.std(ddof=1) / np.sqrt(len(values)))\n    return {\"mean\": center, \"lower95\": center - margin, \"upper95\": center + margin}\n\n\ndef main():\n    # @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n    data = json.loads(DATA.read_text())\n    episodes = data[\"final_evaluation\"][\"evaluation_evidence\"][\"episodes\"]\n    summaries = episodes[0][\"solution\"][\"case_summaries\"]\n    results = []\n    for position, reference in enumerate(summaries):\n        records = [episode[\"solution\"][\"cases\"][position] for episode in episodes]\n        assert all(record[\"case\"] == reference[\"case\"] for record in records)\n        truth_values = sorted(set(record[\"truth\"] for record in records))\n        row = {\"case\": reference[\"case\"], \"truths\": truth_values, \"methods\": {}, \"differences\": {}}\n        for method in METHODS:\n            intervals = [record[\"response\"] if method == \"candidate\" else record[\"baselines\"][method] for record in records]\n            widths = np.array([item[\"upper\"] - item[\"lower\"] for item in intervals])\n            covered = np.array([item[\"lower\"] <= record[\"truth\"] <= item[\"upper\"] for item, record in zip(intervals, records)])\n            bounds = binomtest(int(covered.sum()), len(covered)).proportion_ci(method=\"exact\")\n            row[\"methods\"][method] = {\"coverage\": float(covered.mean()), \"covered\": int(covered.sum()),\n                \"coverage_lower95\": float(bounds.low), \"coverage_upper95\": float(bounds.high),\n                \"width\": mean_interval(widths), \"zero_width_count\": int(np.count_nonzero(widths == 0)),\n                \"widths\": widths.tolist()}\n        candidate_widths = np.array(row[\"methods\"][\"candidate\"][\"widths\"])\n        for method in METHODS[1:]:\n            row[\"differences\"][method] = mean_interval(candidate_widths - row[\"methods\"][method][\"widths\"])\n            recorded = reference[\"comparisons\"][method][\"difference\"]\n            assert np.isclose(row[\"differences\"][method][\"mean\"], recorded[\"mean_difference\"], atol=1e-12)\n            assert np.isclose(row[\"differences\"][method][\"lower95\"], recorded[\"lower95\"], atol=1e-10)\n        results.append(row)\n    out = {\"repetitions\": len(episodes), \"seeds\": [episode[\"seed\"] for episode in episodes],\n           \"case_count\": len(results), \"cases\": results,\n           \"interpretation\": \"Pointwise exact binomial coverage intervals; paired t width-difference intervals. No multiplicity correction or new evaluation.\"}\n    path = ROOT / \"analysis_results.json\"\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    provenance(path)\n    headers = \"Condition & Score control & PPI++ & PPI & Label normal & Exact binomial\"\n    coverage_rows = [headers + r\" \\\\\", r\"\\midrule\"]\n    width_rows = [headers + r\" \\\\\", r\"\\midrule\"]\n    for row in results:\n        coverage_rows.append(\"C%d & \" % row[\"case\"] + \" & \".join(f'{row[\"methods\"][method][\"coverage\"]:.3f}' for method in METHODS) + r\" \\\\\")\n        width_rows.append(\"C%d & \" % row[\"case\"] + \" & \".join(f'{row[\"methods\"][method][\"width\"][\"mean\"]:.5f}' for method in METHODS) + r\" \\\\\")\n    for name, rows in [(\"coverage\", coverage_rows), (\"width\", width_rows)]:\n        path = ROOT / \"tables\" / f\"{name}.tex\"\n        path.write_text(\"% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(rows) + \"\\n\\\\bottomrule\\n\")\n        provenance(path)\n    extended = []\n    for row in results:\n        for method, label in zip(METHODS, LABELS):\n            value = row[\"methods\"][method]\n            extended.append(f'C{row[\"case\"]} & {label} & {value[\"coverage\"]:.3f} [{value[\"coverage_lower95\"]:.3f}, {value[\"coverage_upper95\"]:.3f}] & {value[\"width\"][\"mean\"]:.5f} & {value[\"zero_width_count\"]}' + r\" \\\\\")\n        extended.append(r\"\\midrule\")\n    path = ROOT / \"tables\" / \"complete.tex\"\n    path.write_text(\"% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(extended) + \"\\n\\\\bottomrule\\n\")\n    provenance(path)\n    differences = []\n    for row in results:\n        for method, label in zip(METHODS[1:], LABELS[1:]):\n            value = row[\"differences\"][method]\n            differences.append(f'C{row[\"case\"]} & {label} & {value[\"mean\"]:+.6f} & [{value[\"lower95\"]:+.6f}, {value[\"upper95\"]:+.6f}]' + r\" \\\\\")\n        differences.append(r\"\\midrule\")\n    path = ROOT / \"tables\" / \"differences.tex\"\n    path.write_text(\"% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n\" + \"\\n\".join(differences) + \"\\n\\\\bottomrule\\n\")\n    provenance(path)\n    plt.rcParams.update({\"font.size\": 9, \"axes.titlesize\": 9, \"axes.labelsize\": 9,\n                         \"xtick.labelsize\": 8.5, \"ytick.labelsize\": 9,\n                         \"axes.spines.top\": False, \"axes.spines.right\": False,\n                         \"pdf.fonttype\": 42, \"ps.fonttype\": 42})\n    plotted = [0, 1, 3, 4]\n    figure, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(5.5, 4.3), gridspec_kw={\"width_ratios\": [1, 1.1]})\n    for group_index, indices in enumerate([range(4), range(4, 7)]):\n        coverage_axis, width_axis = axes[group_index]\n        offsets = np.linspace(-.23, .23, len(plotted))\n        for method_index, offset in zip(plotted, offsets):\n            for local_index, case_index in enumerate(indices):\n                value = results[case_index][\"methods\"][METHODS[method_index]]\n                coverage_axis.errorbar(value[\"coverage\"], local_index + offset,\n                    xerr=[[value[\"coverage\"] - value[\"coverage_lower95\"]], [value[\"coverage_upper95\"] - value[\"coverage\"]]],\n                    fmt=\"o\", ms=3.4, lw=.8, color=COLORS[method_index], capsize=1.5)\n        for method_index, offset in zip([1, 3, 4], [-.18, 0, .18]):\n            for local_index, case_index in enumerate(indices):\n                value = results[case_index][\"differences\"][METHODS[method_index]]\n                width_axis.errorbar(1000 * value[\"mean\"], local_index + offset,\n                    xerr=[[1000 * (value[\"mean\"] - value[\"lower95\"])], [1000 * (value[\"upper95\"] - value[\"mean\"])]],\n                    fmt=\"o\", ms=3.4, lw=.8, color=COLORS[method_index], capsize=1.5)\n        for axis in [coverage_axis, width_axis]:\n            axis.set_yticks(range(len(indices)), [f\"C{position + 1}\" for position in indices])\n            axis.set_ylim(len(indices)-.5, -.5)\n            axis.grid(axis=\"x\", alpha=.13)\n        coverage_axis.axvline(.95, ls=\"--\", lw=.8, color=\"#444444\")\n        coverage_axis.set_xlim((.84, 1.005) if group_index == 0 else (.48, 1.015))\n        width_axis.axvline(0, ls=\"--\", lw=.8, color=\"#444444\")\n    axes[0, 0].set_title(\"(a) Coverage: C1–C4\", loc=\"left\")\n    axes[0, 1].set_title(\"(b) Width differences: C1–C4\", loc=\"left\")\n    axes[1, 0].set_title(\"(c) Coverage: C5–C7\", loc=\"left\")\n    axes[1, 1].set_title(\"(d) Width differences: C5–C7\", loc=\"left\")\n    axes[1, 0].set_xlabel(\"Empirical coverage\")\n    axes[1, 1].set_xlabel(\"Width difference (×10⁻³)\")\n    handles = [plt.Line2D([], [], color=COLORS[index], marker=\"o\", ms=4, lw=1, label=LABELS[index]) for index in plotted]\n    figure.legend(handles=handles, loc=\"upper center\", ncol=2, frameon=False, fontsize=9, bbox_to_anchor=(.51, 1.005))\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.09, right=.98, bottom=.13, top=.79, wspace=.46, hspace=.62)\n    save_panel(figure, \"coverage_width_comparison\")\n    figure, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(5.5, 2.3), gridspec_kw={\"width_ratios\": [1.25, 1]})\n    rare = results[4]\n    for method_index in [0, 1, 2, 4]:\n        values = np.sort(rare[\"methods\"][METHODS[method_index]][\"widths\"])\n        axes[0].step(np.r_[0, values], np.r_[0, np.arange(1, len(values)+1)/len(values)], where=\"post\", color=COLORS[method_index], lw=1.25, label=LABELS[method_index])\n    axes[0].set(xlabel=\"Interval width\", ylabel=\"Empirical CDF\", ylim=(0, 1.03), xlim=(0, None))\n    axes[0].set_title(\"(a) C5 width distribution\", loc=\"left\")\n    selected = [0, 1, 2, 4]\n    counts = [rare[\"methods\"][METHODS[index]][\"zero_width_count\"] for index in selected]\n    axes[1].barh(range(4), counts, color=[COLORS[index] for index in selected], height=.6)\n    axes[1].set_yticks(range(4), [LABELS[index] for index in selected], fontsize=8.5)\n    axes[1].invert_yaxis()\n    axes[1].set_xlim(0, max(counts)*1.25)\n    axes[1].set_xlabel(\"Zero-width intervals\")\n    for position, count in enumerate(counts):\n        axes[1].text(count + 2, position, str(count), va=\"center\", fontsize=9)\n    axes[1].set_title(\"(b) Collapse counts\", loc=\"left\")\n    handles, labels = axes[0].get_legend_handles_labels()\n    figure.legend(handles, labels, loc=\"upper center\", ncol=4, frameon=False, fontsize=8.5, bbox_to_anchor=(.5, 1.015), handlelength=1.2, columnspacing=.9)\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.1, right=.99, bottom=.24, top=.73, wspace=.67)\n    save_panel(figure, \"rare_outcome_diagnostic\")\n    concept = ROOT / \"figures\" / \"frozen_score_overview.png\"\n    prompt_log = concept.with_suffix(\".prompts.json\")\n    if not (ROOT / \".concept_figure_complete\").exists() and not concept.exists():\n        from PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n        image = Image.new(\"RGB\", (2400, 630), \"white\")\n        draw = ImageDraw.Draw(image)\n        draw.text((50, 280), \"Concept figure reserved for synchronous rendering\", fill=\"#666666\")\n        image.save(concept)\n    if not prompt_log.exists():\n        prompt_log.write_text(\"{}\\n\")\n    figures = []\n    specifications = {item[\"figure_id\"]: item for item in\n                      json.loads((ROOT / \"paper_strategy.json\").read_text())[\"figure_specs\"]}\n    for name, panels, categories, series, height in [\n        (\"frozen_score_overview\", 1, 4, 2, 1.8),\n        (\"coverage_width_comparison\", 4, 4, 4, 4.3),\n        (\"rare_outcome_diagnostic\", 2, 4, 4, 2.3)]:\n        entry = {\"figure_id\": name, \"path_png\": f\"figures/{name}.png\",\n                 \"figure_type\": specifications[name][\"figure_type\"],\n                 \"n_panels\": panels, \"panels_per_row\": 1 if panels == 1 else 2,\n                 \"categories_per_panel\": [categories] * panels, \"series_per_panel\": [series] * panels,\n                 \"max_label_chars\": 30, \"font_sizes\": {\"title\": 9, \"axis\": 9, \"legend\": 8.5, \"ticks\": 8.5},\n                 \"uses_abbrev_labels\": True, \"uses_progression\": False,\n                 \"source_ids\": [] if panels == 1 else [\"final.evidence.episodes\"],\n                 \"generator\": \"generate-concept-figure\" if panels == 1 else \"matplotlib\",\n                 \"placement\": \"full_width\", \"intended_latex_width_fraction\": 1.0,\n                 \"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\": 8.5}\n        if panels == 1:\n            entry[\"prompt_log_path\"] = f\"figures/{name}.prompts.json\"\n        else:\n            entry[\"path_pdf\"] = f\"figures/{name}.pdf\"\n        figures.append(entry)\n    (ROOT / \"figure_manifest.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\"figures\": figures}, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    for row in results:\n        print(\"C\", row[\"case\"], \"truth\", row[\"truths\"], \"coverage\", row[\"methods\"][\"candidate\"][\"coverage\"], \"width\", row[\"methods\"][\"candidate\"][\"width\"][\"mean\"], \"PPI++ difference\", row[\"differences\"][METHODS[1]])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n--- LOCAL VALIDATION ---\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport jsonschema\nimport pymupdf\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\n\ndef main():\n    data = json.loads((ROOT / \"paper_data.json\").read_text())\n    strategy = json.loads((ROOT / \"paper_strategy.json\").read_text())\n    manifest = json.loads((ROOT / \"figure_manifest.json\").read_text())\n    schema = json.loads((ROOT / \".codex/skills/validate-paper/templates/figure_manifest.schema.json\").read_text())\n    jsonschema.validate(manifest, schema)\n    specifications = {item[\"figure_id\"]: item for item in strategy[\"figure_specs\"]}\n    manuscript = (ROOT / \"paper.tex\").read_text()\n    declared_paths = set()\n    for figure in manifest[\"figures\"]:\n        spec = specifications[figure[\"figure_id\"]]\n        assert figure[\"figure_type\"] == spec[\"figure_type\"], figure[\"figure_id\"]\n        assert figure[\"n_panels\"] <= spec[\"max_panels\"]\n        assert max(figure[\"categories_per_panel\"]) <= spec[\"max_categories_per_panel\"]\n        assert max(figure[\"series_per_panel\"]) <= spec[\"max_series_per_panel\"]\n        assert figure[\"panels_per_row\"] <= spec[\"max_panels_per_row\"]\n        assert figure[\"estimated_min_rendered_font_pt\"] >= 8\n        assert set(figure[\"source_ids\"]) <= set(data[\"grounding_sources\"])\n        for field in [\"path_png\", \"path_pdf\", \"prompt_log_path\"]:\n            if field in figure:\n                assert (ROOT / figure[field]).is_file()\n                declared_paths.add(figure[field])\n    for included in re.findall(r\"\\\\includegraphics(?:\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\{([^}]+)\\}\", manuscript):\n        assert included in declared_paths, included\n    assert set(specifications) == {item[\"figure_id\"] for item in manifest[\"figures\"]}\n    resolved_json = 0\n    resolved_lines = 0\n    for token in re.findall(r\"@evidence\\[\\[([^\\]]+)\\]\\]\", manuscript):\n        target, separator, locator = token.partition(\"#\")\n        path = ROOT / target\n        assert path.is_file(), token\n        if path.suffix == \".json\" and locator.startswith(\"/\"):\n            value = json.loads(path.read_text())\n            for part in locator[1:].split(\"/\"):\n                part = part.replace(\"~1\", \"/\").replace(\"~0\", \"~\")\n                value = value[int(part)] if isinstance(value, list) else value[part]\n            resolved_json += 1\n        if re.fullmatch(r\"L\\d+(?:-L?\\d+)?\", locator):\n            numbers = [int(value) for value in re.findall(r\"\\d+\", locator)]\n            assert max(numbers) <= len(path.read_text().splitlines()), token\n            resolved_lines += 1\n    pdf = pymupdf.open(ROOT / \"paper.pdf\")\n    texts = [page.get_text() for page in pdf]\n    reference_index = next(index for index, text in enumerate(texts) if re.search(r\"\\bREFERENCES\\b\", text))\n    supplement_index = next(index for index, text in enumerate(texts) if \"SUPPLEMENTARY INFORMATION\" in text)\n    assert reference_index in [8, 9], reference_index\n    assert supplement_index > reference_index\n    assert \"LLM USAGE\" in \"\\n\".join(texts)\n    forbidden = r\"\\b(?:ideas?|programs?|attempts?|eligible|worker_01|worker_02|combined_score|rubric)\\b\"\n    for page_text in texts:\n        scrubbed = re.sub(r\"program\\.py\", \"source-file\", page_text)\n        assert not re.search(forbidden, scrubbed, re.I), re.search(forbidden, scrubbed, re.I)\n    body_last = pdf[reference_index - 1]\n    rectangles = []\n    for block in body_last.get_text(\"dict\")[\"blocks\"]:\n        for line in block.get(\"lines\", []):\n            spans = [span for span in line[\"spans\"] if span[\"bbox\"][0] >= 106 and span[\"bbox\"][2] <= 506\n                     and 70 <= span[\"bbox\"][1] < 730 and not span[\"text\"].isdigit()]\n            rectangles.extend(span[\"bbox\"] for span in spans)\n    extent = max(rectangle[3] for rectangle in rectangles) - min(rectangle[1] for rectangle in rectangles)\n    fill = extent / 648\n    assert fill >= .75 if reference_index == 8 else True\n    specification = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"rendered_si\", ROOT / \".codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_rendered_si.py\")\n    validator = importlib.util.module_from_spec(specification)\n    specification.loader.exec_module(validator)\n    body_texts = [page.get_text(clip=pymupdf.Rect(105, 65, 507, 750), sort=True) for page in pdf]\n    errors = validator.validate_rendered_supplementary_information(body_texts)\n    assert not errors, errors\n    summary = json.loads((ROOT / \"scientific-evidence/verification-report.json\").read_text())[\"summary\"]\n    assert summary[\"dangling_references\"] == 0\n    report = {\"status\": \"local_checks_passed\", \"body_pages\": reference_index, \"total_pages\": len(pdf),\n              \"last_body_page_vertical_extent_fraction\": fill,\n              \"geometry_note\": \"Local text-span extent, excluding margin counters; not the parent orchestrator's authoritative occupancy metric.\",\n              \"figure_schema\": \"passed\", \"strategy_figure_budgets\": \"passed\", \"figures\": len(manifest[\"figures\"]),\n              \"resolved_manuscript_json_pointers\": resolved_json, \"resolved_source_line_locators\": resolved_lines,\n              \"rendered_supplement\": \"passed canonical heading/content function on PyMuPDF text within the official text frame\",\n              \"dangling_evidence_references\": 0,\n              \"canonical_tooling_limits\": [\n                  \"Standalone figure-validator entrypoint cannot import the absent parent src.orchestrator module; canonical JSON schema and strategy budgets checked locally.\",\n                  \"compile_latex.sh recorder checker rejects a system texmf.cnf symlink crossing two approved TeX roots. Sanitized pdflatex/BibTeX commands compile successfully; parent revalidation remains authoritative.\",\n                  \"System pdftotext is unavailable. Rendered SI checked from independent PyMuPDF extraction within the official text frame, excluding margin counters.\",\n                  \"Concept image is an orchestrator-owned placeholder until synchronous post-draft rendering.\"\n              ]}\n    (ROOT / \"local_validation_report.json\").write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=2) + \"\\n\")\n    print(json.dumps(report, indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n--- CONCEPT SOURCE CANDIDATES ---\n./paper_repair_prompt_round_1.md:852:8. Because the orchestrator renders the concept figure after this stage, you never need to probe `drawio` / `OPENAI_API_KEY` availability for it. If the orchestrator cannot produce the figure, the manuscript still compiles with your placeholder; do not block on it.\n./paper_evidence_audit.json:22:    \"evidence-source/figures/frozen_score_overview.prompts.json\": \"0bd659c9197393349b0779a77a04104a9ba11bba8059b9372df24f936d2cda6d\",\n./paper_evidence_audit.json:123:    \"figure-asset/figures/frozen_score_overview.png\": \"044b3e2c96f3409741f408367a5a797c62539a4c1a2c0c0d0c3c5d0536240a0e\",\n./paper_evidence_audit.json:135:    \"validator-input/figures/frozen_score_overview.prompts.json\": \"0bd659c9197393349b0779a77a04104a9ba11bba8059b9372df24f936d2cda6d\"\n./paper_evidence_audit_packet.md:746:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth,height=1.8in,keepaspectratio]{figures/frozen_score_overview.png}\n./scripts/build_artifacts.py:166:    concept = ROOT / \"figures\" / \"frozen_score_overview.png\"\n./scripts/build_artifacts.py:169:        from PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n./scripts/build_artifacts.py:171:        draw = ImageDraw.Draw(image)\n./scripts/build_artifacts.py:180:        (\"frozen_score_overview\", 1, 4, 2, 1.8),\n./paper_prompt.md:806:8. Because the orchestrator renders the concept figure after this stage, you never need to probe `drawio` / `OPENAI_API_KEY` availability for it. If the orchestrator cannot produce the figure, the manuscript still compiles with your placeholder; do not block on it.\n./figure_manifest.json:10:      \"figure_id\": \"frozen_score_overview\",\n./figure_manifest.json:23:      \"path_png\": \"figures/frozen_score_overview.png\",\n./figure_manifest.json:25:      \"prompt_log_path\": \"figures/frozen_score_overview.prompts.json\",\n./paper_strategy.json:66:      \"figure_id\": \"frozen_score_overview\",\n./paper_strategy.md:64:### Figure 1 — `frozen_score_overview`\n./REPRODUCIBILITY.md:35:| Concept overview | Synchronous external concept workflow | `figures/frozen_score_overview.png` and prompt log |\n./.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md:10:Generate one reader-facing conceptual overview figure for the paper when a high-level glance-value visual will clarify the method, comparison story, or evidence structure. The figure is produced by the Autoillustrate pipeline (the `autoillustrate` npm release pinned in the agent image): each panel is a collision-checked, deterministically laid-out draw.io diagram, the panels are composed into a single editable `.drawio` file, and the composite is optionally restyled into a camera-ready PNG. The deliverable is a real `.drawio` source plus its export — only the final restyle pass touches a generative model.\n./.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md:21:- **`drawio` desktop CLI** on `PATH` (headless export). Without it Phases 2/4 cannot export.\n./.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md:59:- `full_figure.drawio` — editable draw.io source\n./.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md:64:With `--output` set, the pipeline also copies the best available figure (the enhanced export when Phase 5 ran, otherwise the deterministic export) to `./figures/<figure_id>.png` and drops the plan beside it as `./figures/<figure_id>.prompts.json`. The pipeline does not emit a PDF; the editable `full_figure.drawio` stays in the run workdir.\n./.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md:75:The editable `full_figure.drawio` stays in the run workdir so the figure can be re-edited later. The pipeline produces no PDF; the manifest does not require one for this figure.\n./.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md:79:8. If a prerequisite is missing (for example, no `drawio` CLI) or the pipeline fails, log an explicit skip/failure reason in both `./memory.md` and `./global_memory/memory.md` before falling back to another figure implementation. Apply the same fallback logging rule if the generated figure is too poor to use.\n./.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md:81:9. If you fall back to a non-drawio overview figure, record that fallback reason in the matching `figure_manifest.json` note so the run leaves a clear breadcrumb.\n./.codex/skills/generate-concept-figure/SKILL.md:88:- Editable source preserved at `runs/<ts>/figures/full_figure.drawio`\n./paper_evidence_audit_input_sha256.json:19:  \"evidence-source/figures/frozen_score_overview.prompts.json\": \"0bd659c9197393349b0779a77a04104a9ba11bba8059b9372df24f936d2cda6d\",\n./paper_evidence_audit_input_sha256.json:120:  \"figure-asset/figures/frozen_score_overview.png\": \"044b3e2c96f3409741f408367a5a797c62539a4c1a2c0c0d0c3c5d0536240a0e\",\n./paper_evidence_audit_input_sha256.json:132:  \"validator-input/figures/frozen_score_overview.prompts.json\": \"0bd659c9197393349b0779a77a04104a9ba11bba8059b9372df24f936d2cda6d\"\n./paper.fls:197:INPUT ./figures/frozen_score_overview.png\n./paper.fls:198:INPUT ./figures/frozen_score_overview.png\n./paper.fls:199:INPUT ./figures/frozen_score_overview.png\n./paper.fls:200:INPUT ./figures/frozen_score_overview.png\n./paper.fls:201:INPUT ./figures/frozen_score_overview.png\n./paper.tex:53:\\includegraphics[width=\\textwidth,height=1.8in,keepaspectratio]{figures/frozen_score_