nal | scope=paper\n- summary: paper.tex and claims_grounding.json are consistent with grounded inputs; the anonymous ICLR 2026 draft, PDF, quantitative figures, source archive, and reproduction guide are written.\n- evidence: Final PDF has eight body pages, two reference pages and substantive Supplementary Information including LLM Usage. All 25 citation keys validate, 110 claims map to valid evidence/provenance IDs, 32 manuscript JSON pointers and 17 source-line locators resolve in the local audit, and scientific-evidence has zero dangling references. Final qualification is reported independently as completed/qualified without turning it into a nominal-validity guarantee. C2-only PPI++ narrowing, six widenings, C5 undercoverage/collapse, inconclusive C5 exact-binomial width comparison, missing generators/sample sizes/ablation, and unverified final source identity remain explicit. Visual inspection confirms the final body page is substantially filled and figures use vector exports. No new scientific evaluation was run.\n- next_action: Orchestrator should render the reserved concept figure synchronously and perform its authoritative final compile/layout validation. Canonical tooling limitations are documented in local_validation_report.json; end-to-end experiment reproduction remains unavailable rather than fabricated.\n\n### 2026-11-07T05:37:56.486878+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: Draft citation-gap analysis completed with status no_gaps; no retrieval or manuscript rewrite is justified. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=The audit confirms existing citation coverage without adding or refining a scientific research recommendation.\n- evidence: Wrote draft_reference_gaps.md and draft_reference_gaps.json. All 25 cited keys resolve in bibliography and provenance; paragraph review finds direct support for comparator families, fitted controls and boundary/concentration context. JSON contract validates and SHA-256 checks confirm paper.tex, references.bib and references_provenance.json are unchanged. No reference retrieval performed.\n- next_action: Skip targeted post-draft retrieval; preserve the manuscript scientific-evidence and provenance limitations.\n\n### 2026-11-07T05:38:46.462737+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: Confirmed citation-gap reports with status no_gaps after recovering an unavailable apply_patch wrapper. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=The audit reconfirms existing support without a new scientific recommendation.\n- evidence: Both required reports now exist; JSON structure and matching memo summary validate. Protected manuscript, bibliography and reference-provenance hashes are unchanged. No retrieval performed. The previous log append preceded output creation because the shell lacked fail-fast handling; global logging initially rejected the global_memory symlink, so this append uses its resolved directory.\n- next_action: Skip targeted post-draft retrieval and retain documented experimental limitations.\n\n### 2026-11-07T05:44:24.086100+00:00 | step=paper | scope=paper\n- summary: Repair pass isolates two strategy/manifest figure-type mismatches; manuscript and scientific findings remain stable. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Metadata repair changes no scientific recommendation.\n- evidence: validation_feedback.json reports only coverage_width_comparison and rare_outcome_diagnostic figure_type hard errors; evidence audit passed with zero findings. Independently read final_evaluation: completed/qualified/true; downstream_study and task_names absent.\n- next_action: Align figure type metadata with strategy, prevent recurrence in artifact builder, and rerun grounding, figure and compilation checks.\n\n### 2026-11-07T05:46:13.382475+00:00 | step=verify | scope=paper\n- summary: Normalized quantitative strategy types to canonical composite and added exact strategy/manifest agreement to the local checker. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=Schema alignment preserves every scientific and visual design decision.\n- evidence: Initial direct copying of custom strategy types failed the canonical schema enum. Both quantitative entries now use composite in paper_strategy.json and figure_manifest.json; descriptive content specs, panel budgets, plotted files and concept ownership are unchanged. Builder reads types from the strategy. Sections, 25 citation keys, 110 claims and evidence verification pass with zero dangling links. Canonical figure CLI is unavailable because src.orchestrator is not mounted.\n- next_action: Complete sanitized compilation, confirm manuscript and evidence hashes unchanged, and leave authoritative parent revalidation pending.\n\n### 2026-11-07T05:46:39.308535+00:00 | step=final | scope=paper\n- summary: Targeted figure metadata repair is complete and locally validated; paper.tex and claims_grounding.json remain consistent with grounded inputs. gate=kept; trigger=none; reason=No scientific finding or recommendation changed.\n- evidence: Canonical manifest schema, exact strategy/manifest type agreement, figure budgets, section/citation checks, claim mappings, zero-dangling scientific evidence, sanitized compilation, and independent rendered-SI checks pass. Protected manuscript, claims, evidence registry, bibliography, provenance and numerical analysis hashes are unchanged. Qualification and validity/source/ablation limitations remain intact. repair_validation_report.json records canonical CLI limitations and unchanged soft warnings; no new experiments or retrieval were performed.\n- next_action: Parent orchestrator should rerun authoritative validation; retain existing concept workflow ownership and manuscript limitations.\n\n_idea_generation\nattempts_history.jsonl\nbest_program_manifest.json\nconclusions.md\nconclusions_history.jsonl\nconclusions_other_workers.md\nevents.jsonl\nidea_generation_failures.jsonl\nideas\nideas_history.jsonl\nlatest_run_manifest.json\nmemory.jsonl\nmemory.md\nouter_state.json\ntask\ncat: conclusions.md: No such file or directory\n\n--- PARENT / MODULES ---\nfinal_evaluation\ninvestigation\nmetrics\npaper\npipeline_events.jsonl\ntask\ntask_drafting\n\n--- COMPILE ---\n#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nif [ $# -ne 1 ]; then\n  echo \"Usage: bash compile_latex.sh <paper.tex>\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nTEX_ARGUMENT=\"$1\"\nif [ ! -f \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\" ]; then\n  echo \"Missing TeX file: $TEX_ARGUMENT\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nif ! command -v pdflatex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdflatex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v bibtex >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: bibtex\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: python3\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\nif ! command -v pdftotext >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n  echo \"Missing required command: pdftotext\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPAPER_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\" && pwd)\"\nTEX_FILE=\"$(basename \"$TEX_ARGUMENT\")\"\nBASE=\"${TEX_FILE%.tex}\"\nRECORDER_FILE=\"${BASE}.fls\"\nAUX_FILE=\"${BASE}.aux\"\n\ncd \"$PAPER_DIR\"\n\nrun_sanitized() {\n  python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" run -- \"$@\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex() {\n  rm -f -- \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  set +e\n  run_sanitized pdflatex \\\n    -recorder -no-shell-escape -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error \"$TEX_FILE\"\n  local return_code=$?\n  set -e\n  if [ -f \"$RECORDER_FILE\" ]; then\n    python3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" recorder \\\n      --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --fls \"$RECORDER_FILE\"\n  elif [ \"$return_code\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    echo \"LaTeX recorder output missing: $PAPER_DIR/$RECORDER_FILE\" >&2\n    return 1\n  fi\n  return \"$return_code\"\n}\n\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_compile_inputs.py\" bibtex \\\n  --paper-dir \"$PAPER_DIR\" --aux \"$AUX_FILE\"\nrun_sanitized bibtex \"$BASE\"\nrun_pdflatex\nrun_pdflatex\npython3 \"$SCRIPT_DIR/validate_rendered_si.py\" --pdf \"${BASE}.pdf\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
